  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\n\nhttps://spec.matrix.org/v1.18/appendices/#examples\n\n**Issue**\nThe spec says:\n\n> Given the following JSON object:\n>\n> ```json\n> {\n>     \"a\": -0,\n>     \"b\": 1e10\n> }\n> ```\n> \n> The following canonical JSON should be produced:\n> \n> ```json\n> {\"a\":0,\"b\":10000000000}\n> ```\n\nThis implies that implementations must support the syntax `1e10` on incoming JSON. This was added in #1573, and I think it's incorrect. Synapse does *not* allow it (at least, for sensible room versions that forbid floats in events). I think it is legitimate for implementations to *either* canonicalise to 10000000000, *or* reject the JSON.\n",
